<title>UK: Glaxo Welcome down on pound strength.</title>
<headline>Glaxo Welcome down on pound strength.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in drugs group Glaxo Wellcome Plc fell 11p to 987 on Monday as strength of the pound against the dollar made investors sell here and buy American Depository Receipts (ADRs) instead, market makers said.</p>
<p>&quot;You can buy them cheaper in ADR-form,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>The pound earlier reached a 16-month high, peaking at 1.6145 dollars.</p>
<p>Among other stocks in the pharmaceutical sector, Zeneca was up 11 pence at 1,750, while Medeva edged up 1-1/2 pence to 269-1/2.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
